<p>Read this first. A full replay gives the rest of the track a concrete target: every later lesson explains one part of this interaction. It is not a hand-written ideal conversation. The twenty responses below were captured from a successful live run of <code>HomeInsuranceQuoteFlow</code>, with the test clock frozen to <code>2027-07-15</code>.</p>

<p>The model's collection wording can vary on another run. The tables, quote IDs, validity date, final session state, and completed flag are code-owned assertions. The name and email in the final turn are obvious fixture data, not a customer record.</p>

<h2 id="run-it-yourself">Run it yourself</h2>

<p>From the demo repository, with <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> and <code>PICOFLOW_KEY</code> configured:</p>

<pre><code class="language-bash">cd pico-demo
npm run test:home-insurance-flow</code></pre>

<p>The test starts the Nest application, sends all twenty requests to <code>POST /ai/run</code> with one durable session ID, semantically evaluates every response, and reads the final SQLite session document. It verifies the corrected four-year roof, the $5,000 re-rated deductible, the current Enhanced selection, explicit consent, and <code>completed: true</code> on turn 20.</p>

<p>For a fast provider-free check of the same rating rules:</p>

<p>The live scenario uses credentials from <code>.env</code> and is skipped when they are unavailable.</p>

